  "severity": "critical",
  "host_observations": [
    {"host": "WS-CORP-09.corp.local", "role": "endpoint", "user": "v.borowski", "first_seen": "2032-07-12T17:48:08+0000", "last_seen": "2032-07-12T17:52:30+0000"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Domain recon + LDAP RootDSE bind", "technique": "T1003.006", "what_happened": "At 2032-07-12 17:48:08 UTC on WS-CORP-09, Sysmon EID 1 captured whoami.exe /groups + nltest.exe /dclist:corp.local with parent powershell.exe. AMSI EID 4104 captured a scriptblock issuing LDAP RootDSE bind reading defaultNamingContext + dnsHostName, then enumerating Replicating-Directory-Changes ACEs on the domain root (objectType GUID 1131f6aa-9c07-11d1-f79f-00c04fc2dcd2 / 1131f6ad-9c07-11d1-f79f-00c04fc2dcd2 / 89e95b76-444d-4c62-991a-0facbeda640c).", "chain_reason": "Enumerating the three Replicating-Directory-Changes ACE GUIDs is the DCSync pre-flight: the attacker is checking WHICH identity has the GetChanges + GetChangesAll + GetChangesInFilteredSet rights needed to invoke DRSUAPI replication."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "repadmin /showrepl + /syncall — replication API exercise", "technique": "T1003.006", "what_happened": "At 2032-07-12 17:48:42, Sysmon EID 1 captured repadmin.exe /showrepl then repadmin.exe /syncall /A /e /q with parent powershell.exe.", "chain_reason": "repadmin.exe is normally used by AD engineers from a domain controller. From a workstation (WS-CORP-09) by an interactive user, it is a DRSUAPI replication exercise to test access to the API used by DCSync."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Security 4662 with DS-Replication-Get-Changes GUIDs from non-DC", "technique": "T1003.006", "what_happened": "At 2032-07-12 17:49:14, DC-CORP-01.corp.local Security 4662 (an operation was performed on an object) recorded SubjectUserName=CORP\\v.borowski, AccessMask=0x100 (DS-Control-Access), Properties containing both '1131f6aa-9c07-11d1-f79f-00c04fc2dcd2' (DS-Replication-Get-Changes) AND '1131f6ad-9c07-11d1-f79f-00c04fc2dcd2' (DS-Replication-Get-Changes-All). Source IP 10.40.55.109 (= WS-CORP-09, NOT a DC). Rule 100119 triggered.", "chain_reason": "4662 with the two GetChanges + GetChangesAll GUIDs together, originating from a workstation IP (not a DC peer), is the DEFINITIVE DCSync detection signal — these rights are normally exercised by DCs replicating to each other, never by workstations."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "DRSUAPI RPC + AMSI dcsync tool literals + mimikatz-pattern marker file", "technique": "T1003.006", "what_happened": "At 2032-07-12 17:49:30, Sysmon EID 3 captured outbound TCP from powershell.exe on WS-CORP-09 to DC-CORP-01.corp.local on port 135 (RPC EPM) then a dynamic high-port (DRSUAPI binding). AMSI EID 4104 captured scriptblock literals: 'mimikatz.exe \"lsadump::dcsync /domain:corp.local /user:krbtgt\"', 'Invoke-DCSync -DomainController DC01 -ReplicationUser CORP\\krbtgt', 'secretsdump.py -just-dc-ntlm CORP/Administrator@DC01', 'Get-ADReplAccount -All -Server DC01'. A marker file at C:\\Users\\v.borowski\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p143_dcs_174808\\dcsync_out.txt (256 bytes) contains the literal 'Hash NTLM: 31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0' for the krbtgt RDN. Rule 100120 + 100121 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Outbound DRSUAPI RPC from a workstation to a DC + AMSI mimikatz lsadump::dcsync literal + mimikatz-format marker file showing the krbtgt NTLM hash = DCSync executed and krbtgt hash captured."}
  ],
